          "sessionID": "ses_22",
          "messageID": "msg_02",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "That's because `fetchPosts` is an `async` function, so calling it returns a Promise immediately -- the actual data isn't ready yet when you log it. `async` functions still run on the same thread; they don't hand work off to another thread, they just let other code run while they're waiting. To get the resolved value, you need `await fetchPosts()` (inside another `async` function) instead of logging the call directly."
        },
