          "text": "Same thing here -- `fetchComments` is also `async`, so `fetchComments(postId)` alone gives you the Promise, not the comments. This isn't a different bug, it's the same pattern: any call to an `async` function needs `await` in front of it to get the resolved value, since the function still runs on the same thread and just returns a placeholder until it finishes."
