        {
          "id": "prt_08b",
          "sessionID": "ses_22",
          "messageID": "msg_08",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "No -- JavaScript's event loop is single-threaded. `async`/`await` doesn't spawn a thread; it's syntax for pausing a function at an `await` and letting other code run in the meantime, then resuming once the Promise settles. There's no second thread doing the work in parallel -- that's why forgetting `await` doesn't just make things slower, it hands you the un-settled Promise object itself instead of the data."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_08c",
          "sessionID": "ses_22",
          "messageID": "msg_08",
          "type": "step-finish",
